{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients","id":1540024,"title":"Powers of the Ancients","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-07T18:07:56-07:00","id":1540024,"title":"Powers of the Ancients","content":"How dangerous are the elders and methuselahs really? In the lore it has elders being movers and shakers of entire regions to entire continent's, and yet they seem to die in droves against everything from neonates, to garou, to mages. So is it all just propaganda or do the ancients really have some bite to them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28506-carsusbloodking","name":"Carsusbloodking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T18:35:50-07:00","id":1540026,"title":"","content":"Where did you ever read about them dying in droves, to begin with? And which of the lines you take as the main one for this analysis?<br /> <br /> Elders and Methuselah are first and foremost manipulators in the setting, so the whole dying thing is a bad angle to understand them to begin with. What in-lore the Garou fear when dealing with vampires isn't their combat prowess, but the possibility that they're just being played with by another vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T19:11:20-07:00","id":1540027,"title":"","content":"I dont see them dying in droves anywhere, except perhaps the Gehenna book, and that is against the Antediluvians themselves.<br /> <br /> Everywhere else that they have stats they are either the big bad of the adventure, or part of the threat (most likely there are multiple elders / methuselahs fighting each other, using your characters as pawns).<br /> <br /> By the rules, a prepared high level mage can wipe the floor with most of the stated low generation vampires, but those mages have other mages at the same level of power as their own adversaries. Garou packs could and should take a Wyrm foe like a low humanity low generation Vampire... But this is a task for packs with members at rank 4 and 5, certainly not many of those packs around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 08-08-2024, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T19:58:08-07:00","id":1540030,"title":"","content":"What makes elders and ancients so dangerous besides them being extremely well versed with there in clan Disciplines and out of clan Disciplines is that have built up considerable resources that they can draw upon if they feel vaguely concerned. In addition by this time they have gained the mindset of long term thinking as they grasp that time is on there side and that short term losses that lead to long term gains is okay and opportunities will come again and with minor effort they can position themselves to get what they desire.<br /> <br /> I don't where you get the notion that they are dying in droves? Helena, Critias, Menulas, Montano, Talley, Lucita, Fatima, Vykos and Mithras are still around causing trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 08-09-2024, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T12:35:37-07:00","id":1540059,"title":"","content":"A lot of things can change from game to game when crossovers happen.<br /> <br /> Mages can do a lot of things against any splat. But then, it is up to the ST to decide which defenses the Nightfolk have against Magic. The game simply doesn't expect them to be powerless just because the appropriate traits don't exist in their original game lines.<br /> <br /> So, depending on your decisions, an Elder may go as far as to have effective Arete 7+ for the purpose of countering Magic without the need for any Action to be wasted on this and without interfering with their own powers. They may have effective Permadox to mess with a Mage. Disciplines may have <i>auto-win </i>against opposing effects of a lower Sphere rank.<br /> <br /> Just some examples of rules that appeared in the books at some point to address how dealing with a vampire should really play out for a Mage, and while they're all optional, the books make it clear that using none is also optional, not how the game is supposed to run.<br /> <br /> Elders and Methuselah are meant to be big baddies for all the lines, but how much is an ST call, there's no absolute answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T15:21:06-07:00","id":1540067,"title":"","content":"Most of the elders and ancients will have created potent Amalgam powers that will give them a much needed edge to aid them in most cases and probably didn't share it with there childer or grand childer. Just think of what types of tricks Mithras would have after 3,000+ years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-11T21:56:18-07:00","id":1541946,"title":"","content":"It's described explicitly in the lore: <br /> <br /> &quot;YOU LOSE.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which I never liked. I understand, the developers wanted to weave a sense of dread and paranoia in the game. If you were a virtually an all-powerful demigod who can heal all wounds, have mind control, super strength, super speed, invisibility, etc., with no danger except from furry murder machine tanks outside of the cities, it would be a very boring game.<br /> <br /> This is why they tried to reboot the franchise as Requiem, which I think is a superior game. <br /> <br /> But no, &quot;I lub my Lucita, Talley, and Beckett&quot; crowd rejected it. But parts of it have been incorporated into V5. Which is good, but I think they should have pushed Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-12T13:59:37-07:00","id":1541988,"title":"","content":"As I was more of a fan of the serpent Hesha Rudhze then the above mentioned Kindred, I was saddened that the game was ending and there would be no new stuff about the Follower of Set elder. I tried to create characters in the other games inspired by him but it wasn't the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T09:42:09-07:00","id":1542250,"title":"","content":"Die in droves? Not that ive seen. <br /> <br /> Th old maxim &quot;If it has Stats it can die&quot; may apply but thats up to the ST. With crossovers, its whatever system the ST values more. They will tend to 'win'. <br /> <br /> IMO, killing potent Elders and Ancients is more a story device, not a dungeon to clear.<br /> <br /> The hardest part, is gonna be finding them. They usually have layers and layers of proxies, most unknowingly. Many have faked their death, multiple times. Most will just turn your friends to enemies and ruin shit around you to distract you and bleed your resources. <br /> <br /> Even an Ancient Brujah likely figured out combat is a last resort. Its not very efficient. But it makes an exciting story piece. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T11:10:39-07:00","id":1542258,"title":"","content":"If anything most ancients become more reclusive as they endure for thousands of years and see that being around can breed a certain contempt by there less potent associates and they don't want that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-16T14:46:55-07:00","id":1542272,"title":"","content":"I also wonder how many of them pose as much younger kindred like Helena from Chicago by Night in her Portia guise? That's also a good way to misdirect any intelligent snoops who may seek them out and want to feed on there powerful blood potency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-19T21:18:42-07:00","id":1542442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients?p=1542272#post1542272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also wonder how many of them pose as much younger kindred like Helena from Chicago by Night in her Portia guise? That's also a good way to misdirect any intelligent snoops who may seek them out and want to feed on there powerful blood potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would guess a few do but (lack of) Humanity could give them away. <br /> <br /> I would guess more Ancients would sleep most the time and work through proxies, or swing from identity to identity after a series of faked deaths.<br /> <br /> Ancients with Obfuscate for example, likely would t be found or even remembered. <br /> <br /> I tend to view Ancients, and older, as less characters and more as as abstractions. Nexuses of power that do inscrutable things to keep power and or keep from going fully degenerate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25883-inspectorg","name":"InspectorG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-20T01:47:56-07:00","id":1542450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carsusbloodking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients#post1540024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How dangerous are the elders and methuselahs really? In the lore it has elders being movers and shakers of entire regions to entire continent's, and yet they seem to die in droves against everything from neonates, to garou, to mages. So is it all just propaganda or do the ancients really have some bite to them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the general power level concept (which isn't always backed up mechanically) is that an elder vampire can go toe-to-toe with a werewolf and maybe survive. Truly ancient vampires like Mithras or Baba Yaga can take on an entire pack of werewolves. When you get to Antedeluvians, Set was able to defeat and curse the Silent Striders, permanently exile them from their homeland and cut them off from their ancestor spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-20T09:39:03-07:00","id":1542458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients?p=1542450#post1542450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the general power level concept (which isn't always backed up mechanically)</div> </div> </div> </div>When you never playtest, the mechanics are definitely like a mechanical bull. Some V:tM writer makes a bunch of assumptions with the powers given, but in the W:tA books, Garou can grow 30 feet tall, double their Strength, and enter a super frenzy. And that's not even the full extent of Gifts that can just flat out flip the table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> is that an elder vampire can go toe-to-toe with a werewolf and maybe survive. Truly ancient vampires like Mithras or Baba Yaga can take on an entire pack of werewolves. When you get to Antedeluvians, Set was able to defeat and curse the Silent Striders, permanently exile them from their homeland and cut them off from their ancestor spirits. </div> </div> </div>Sutekh was more of a case of esoteric powers getting around the problem of &quot;Shu Horus can wallop me with One on One, I should find another way&quot;. Mithras is practically in his own setting where nothing makes sense and Baba Yaga is accompanied by sad trombone music due to Nights of Prophecy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-21T14:45:13-07:00","id":1542497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients?p=1542458#post1542458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When you never playtest, the mechanics are definitely like a mechanical bull. Some V:tM writer makes a bunch of assumptions with the powers given, but in the W:tA books, Garou can grow 30 feet tall, double their Strength, and enter a super frenzy. And that's not even the full extent of Gifts that can just flat out flip the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>CofD did a far better job at keeping the relative power of splats within expectations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients?p=1542458#post1542458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sutekh was more of a case of esoteric powers getting around the problem of &quot;Shu Horus can wallop me with One on One, I should find another way&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not so sure that\u2019s the reason, or simply that they wanted to play into the old idea that all magic comes from Egypt, where it was better and cooler.<br /> <br /> That, and/or someone\u2019s love for Howard\u2019s Set.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients?p=1542458#post1542458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mithras is practically in his own setting where nothing makes sense</div> </div> </div> </div>My wife loves Vampire Mithras, I can\u2019t see why.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients?p=1542458#post1542458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Baba Yaga is accompanied by sad trombone music due to Nights of Prophecy.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the whole Silver Fang packs she had under control got accepted back into the fold, because that\u2019s what happens when you spend about 10 years serving the Wyrm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T11:51:23-07:00","id":1542566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients?p=1542497#post1542497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> CofD did a far better job at keeping the relative power of splats within expectations.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>CofD could also be called World of Hindsight, so I hope so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I\u2019m not so sure that\u2019s the reason, or simply that they wanted to play into the old idea that all magic comes from Egypt, where it was better and cooler.<br /> <br /> That, and/or someone\u2019s love for Howard\u2019s Set. </div> </div> </div>Two (or more) things can be true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My wife loves Vampire Mithras, I can\u2019t see why. </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's because all of the metaplot around him is so unhinged and gonzo?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the whole Silver Fang packs she had under control got accepted back into the fold, because that\u2019s what happens when you spend about 10 years serving the Wyrm. </div> </div> </div>Was that in a W:tA book, or Nights of Prophecy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T12:07:23-07:00","id":1542570,"title":"","content":"Women love the bad boys Monteparnas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-24T14:48:26-07:00","id":1542584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients?p=1542570#post1542570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Women love the bad boys Monteparnas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a woman, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients?p=1542566#post1542566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was that in a W:tA book, or Nights of Prophecy?</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC it was in a WtA book, either SF Tribebook or another talking about either the Sept of the Crescent Moon and/or queen Tvarivich.<br /> <br /> While it is a quite detailed memory, though, it was some time ago and not long after reading NoP, so take it with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> Even if it is true, though, I\u2019d say it was probably a means to brush things off instead of devoting a lot of space in the book to explain the mess NoP created.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-29T04:55:51-07:00","id":1542864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients?p=1540059#post1540059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of things can change from game to game when crossovers happen.<br /> <br /> Mages can do a lot of things against any splat. But then, it is up to the ST to decide which defenses the Nightfolk have against Magic. The game simply doesn't expect them to be powerless just because the appropriate traits don't exist in their original game lines.<br /> <br /> So, depending on your decisions, an Elder may go as far as to have effective Arete 7+ for the purpose of countering Magic without the need for any Action to be wasted on this and without interfering with their own powers. They may have effective Permadox to mess with a Mage. Disciplines may have <i>auto-win </i>against opposing effects of a lower Sphere rank.<br /> <br /> Just some examples of rules that appeared in the books at some point to address how dealing with a vampire should really play out for a Mage, and while they're all optional, the books make it clear that using none is also optional, not how the game is supposed to run.<br /> <br /> Elders and Methuselah are meant to be big baddies for all the lines, but how much is an ST call, there's no absolute answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, so much this. Elders and specially Methuselah are meant to be big baddies for all lines. It's funny how often this kind of topic arises, with people &quot;making fun&quot; of how weak are vampires compared to mage and werewolves. The thing I always say is that vampires are much weaker in fact at the bottom (as I have explained sometimes around this forum in the past, mage and werewolf start from another premise entirely and they begin in a much better position than vampires, but this has to do with many factors), but at the very top there are very few things that can compete with them.<br /> It's interesting because this is just a players thing and mostly found among new players, because the setting gives a totally different vibe, e.g. just look at what Rage Across Russia states about Baba Yaga.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 09-29-2024, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T01:57:51-07:00","id":1542897,"title":"","content":"A huge problem, in my opinion, is the result of an immaturity in understanding that there is a difference between the lore, the narrative, and the mechanical rules.<br /> <br /> From a mechanical rules perspective, Mages are probably the strongest among the splats of the game. This isn\u2019t necessarily true from a lore standpoint. People assume that the bad balance in the rules (because it is bad balance) is representative of a narrative reality.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s no coincidence that Chronicles of Darkness put in a lot of work to ensure cross-splat balance.<br /> <br /> Even the recent editions, having realized this, made a huge effort to reduce the mechanical overpoweredness of Mages: now, starting from M20, the Night Folk are all given a countermagic value equal to their Wits + Occult. This means that many Methuselahs are practically made of primium. The same goes for mental magics: now manipulating the mind of a vampire is done with a difficulty ranging from +3 to +8.<br /> <br /> In lore, the Methuselahs are at the top of the existential threats in the World of Darkness. When Baba Yaga emerged, she destroyed entire Werewolf Caerns, subjugated multiple Mages, and overthrew the Technocracy. Half of what Baba Yaga did would have made a good portion of Archmages explode into a smoking cloud of Paradox (Zmej? The Shadow Curtain?).<br /> <br /> The Tremere survived the first Massasa War, and during the Second, the Tremere decimated House Thigh, Tytalus, and Flamebeu (this is from Mage manuals). And it doesn\u2019t seem like the Order was very calm when Tremere manifested in front of them at the end of <i>Blood Treachery</i>.<br /> <br /> Even in <i>Book of Chantries</i>, ancient vampires are identified as excellent adversaries for Mage chantries, even powerful ones.<br /> <br /> Even in Werewolf ancient vampires are often the big bad: Odin Is the epitomic enemy of the Get of Fenrir, the Tzimisce managed to fend off the Shadow Lords, and ask the Silent Striders if It's true that Vampires are pushovers.<br /> <br /> However, there is a group of players who confuse the mechanics (unbalanced and later revised by the authors themselves) with the narrative canon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T03:44:38-07:00","id":1542900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients?p=1542897#post1542897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A huge problem, in my opinion, is the result of an immaturity in understanding that there is a difference between the lore, the narrative, and the mechanical rules.<br /> <br /> From a mechanical rules perspective, Mages are probably the strongest among the splats of the game. This isn\u2019t necessarily true from a lore standpoint. People assume that the bad balance in the rules (because it is bad balance) is representative of a narrative reality.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s no coincidence that Chronicles of Darkness put in a lot of work to ensure cross-splat balance.<br /> <br /> Even the recent editions, having realized this, made a huge effort to reduce the mechanical overpoweredness of Mages: now, starting from M20, the Night Folk are all given a countermagic value equal to their Wits + Occult. This means that many Methuselahs are practically made of primium. The same goes for mental magics: now manipulating the mind of a vampire is done with a difficulty ranging from +3 to +8.<br /> <br /> In lore, the Methuselahs are at the top of the existential threats in the World of Darkness. When Baba Yaga emerged, she destroyed entire Werewolf Caerns, subjugated multiple Mages, and overthrew the Technocracy. Half of what Baba Yaga did would have made a good portion of Archmages explode into a smoking cloud of Paradox (Zmej? The Shadow Curtain?).<br /> <br /> The Tremere survived the first Massasa War, and during the Second, the Tremere decimated House Thigh, Tytalus, and Flamebeu (this is from Mage manuals). And it doesn\u2019t seem like the Order was very calm when Tremere manifested in front of them at the end of <i>Blood Treachery</i>.<br /> <br /> Even in <i>Book of Chantries</i>, ancient vampires are identified as excellent adversaries for Mage chantries, even powerful ones.<br /> <br /> Even in Werewolf ancient vampires are often the big bad: Odin Is the epitomic enemy of the Get of Fenrir, the Tzimisce managed to fend off the Shadow Lords, and ask the Silent Striders if It's true that Vampires are pushovers.<br /> <br /> However, there is a group of players who confuse the mechanics (unbalanced and later revised by the authors themselves) with the narrative canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't have said better than you did. A resist roll was necessary since the beginning for many things in the line, especially regarding cross overs, as as much as I love werewolf and mage, while the latter has a very good system for powers (I'd say one of the best ever created in the forms of Spheres), with the former it isn't the case at all. I love werewolf, don't get me wrong, but there are so many totally non-sense gifts that one friend of mine used to joke that they came up with some of those ideas thinking that nobody would ever use them, because the amount of &quot;one-win button&quot; in the form of gifts is saddening for a game and uiverse so cool as werewolf, I mean a resist roll is always welcomed in this sort of situation, like one of the most infamous examples &quot;Paws of a newborn cub&quot;, I mean which ST in his right state of mind wouldn't make a resist roll for the one on the receiving end of the power!? The power is terribly designed for this reason alone, it's not tematic at all and it feels like a carelessly designed power just for the sake of powerplay. It would make any antagonist or PC, for the matter, useless, reducing an epic battle to a ridiculous single dice roll. Of all WoD powers I know (and at this point I'm pretty confident I know every single power in the game) this one deserves the cake for the worst ofender in terms of any notion of balance, as I said, it's like the guy who came up with it thought that it was never going to be used, so &quot;why bother&quot;. Every ST I know house rule it.<br /> <br /> I only have to add as well that, I'm actually a fan of all splats, I have a lot of experience sstorytelling all game lines (Mainly Vampire, Mage and Werewolf, but I attempted Dark Ages Fay once) since I was a kid, for more than 2 decades and as such, I only have to add that I think Night Folk counter magic in M20 was a bit over the top. I mean, because as it is, even mighty Porthos or Voormas seem a bit powerless against the likes of Mithras, Baba Yaga or Goratrix, to cite a few examples. I think they went a bit too far with the Wits + Occult countermagic and I have a hard time adapting it to my crossover games, because it tend to make mage players feel a bit offended and powerless (with reason), especially since Wits + Occult, for instance, goes easily beyond 10 and Arete goes theorically until 10, but in practice it almost never ever gets past 6 or 7.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T08:14:19-07:00","id":1542907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients?p=1542897#post1542897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A huge problem, in my opinion, is the result of an immaturity in understanding that there is a difference between the lore, the narrative, and the mechanical rules.<br /> <br /> From a mechanical rules perspective, Mages are probably the strongest among the splats of the game. This isn\u2019t necessarily true from a lore standpoint. People assume that the bad balance in the rules (because it is bad balance) is representative of a narrative reality.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s no coincidence that Chronicles of Darkness put in a lot of work to ensure cross-splat balance.<br /> <br /> Even the recent editions, having realized this, made a huge effort to reduce the mechanical overpoweredness of Mages: now, starting from M20, the Night Folk are all given a countermagic value equal to their Wits + Occult. This means that many Methuselahs are practically made of primium. The same goes for mental magics: now manipulating the mind of a vampire is done with a difficulty ranging from +3 to +8.</div> </div> </div> </div>Primium isn't so impressive, though that's another problem with having people who don't do math designing systems (difficulty 8 is a rather high hurdle for the paltry sum of dice that primium usually gives; even doubled successes can't compensate for that).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In lore, the Methuselahs are at the top of the existential threats in the World of Darkness. When Baba Yaga emerged, she destroyed entire Werewolf Caerns, subjugated multiple Mages, and overthrew the Technocracy. Half of what Baba Yaga did would have made a good portion of Archmages explode into a smoking cloud of Paradox (Zmej? The Shadow Curtain?). </div> </div> </div>That's kind of unique to Baba Yaga, since she was a former mage and still had control over the Zmei due to the means of their summoning for some reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Tremere survived the first Massasa War, and during the Second, the Tremere decimated House Thigh, Tytalus, and Flamebeu (this is from Mage manuals). And it doesn\u2019t seem like the Order was very calm when Tremere manifested in front of them at the end of <i>Blood Treachery</i>.<br /> <br /> Even in <i>Book of Chantries</i>, ancient vampires are identified as excellent adversaries for Mage chantries, even powerful ones. </div> </div> </div>Time for a party. Time for lawn chairs!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even in Werewolf ancient vampires are often the big bad: Odin Is the epitomic enemy of the Get of Fenrir, the Tzimisce managed to fend off the Shadow Lords, and ask the Silent Striders if It's true that Vampires are pushovers. </div> </div> </div>I assume that this was just the perception of V:tM writers viewing it as the &quot;main line&quot; and trying to get everyone to donate to their lotion fund.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, there is a group of players who confuse the mechanics (unbalanced and later revised by the authors themselves) with the narrative canon. </div> </div> </div>How much later are we talking? It became horridly difficult for vampires of all generations to soak agg in Revised, and V20 didn't change that. The assumption seems to be &quot;even if you're an ancient, stay in the background or something is going to cap your ass.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I couldn't have said better than you did. A resist roll was necessary since the beginning for many things in the line, especially regarding cross overs, as as much as I love werewolf and mage, while the latter has a very good system for powers (I'd say one of the best ever created in the forms of Spheres), with the former it isn't the case at all. I love werewolf, don't get me wrong, but there are so many totally non-sense gifts that one friend of mine used to joke that they came up with some of those ideas thinking that nobody would ever use them, because the amount of &quot;one-win button&quot; in the form of gifts is saddening for a game and uiverse so cool as werewolf, I mean a resist roll is always welcomed in this sort of situation, like one of the most infamous examples &quot;Paws of a newborn cub&quot;, I mean which ST in his right state of mind wouldn't make a resist roll for the one on the receiving end of the power!? The power is terribly designed for this reason alone, it's not tematic at all and it feels like a carelessly designed power just for the sake of powerplay.</div> </div> </div> </div>The theme of PotNB is &quot;If you take a swing at the king, you'd best not miss.&quot; It was meant to make people wonder if, perhaps, the Silver Fangs do have some higher favor on their side.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It would make any antagonist or PC, for the matter, useless, reducing an epic battle to a ridiculous single dice roll. Of all WoD powers I know (and at this point I'm pretty confident I know every single power in the game) this one deserves the cake for the worst ofender in terms of any notion of balance, as I said, it's like the guy who came up with it thought that it was never going to be used, so &quot;why bother&quot;. Every ST I know house rule it. </div> </div> </div>How many STs? Because, again, it didn't change for the 20th anniversary edition, even though a lot of Gifts actually had a silver Achilles heel added in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I only have to add as well that, I'm actually a fan of all splats, I have a lot of experience sstorytelling all game lines (Mainly Vampire, Mage and Werewolf, but I attempted Dark Ages Fay once) since I was a kid, for more than 2 decades and as such, I only have to add that I think Night Folk counter magic in M20 was a bit over the top. I mean, because as it is, even mighty Porthos or Voormas seem a bit powerless against the likes of Mithras, Baba Yaga or Goratrix, to cite a few examples. I think they went a bit too far with the Wits + Occult countermagic and I have a hard time adapting it to my crossover games, because it tend to make mage players feel a bit offended and powerless (with reason), especially since Wits + Occult, for instance, goes easily beyond 10 and Arete goes theorically until 10, but in practice it almost never ever gets past 6 or 7. </div> </div> </div>If it uses Occult, they actually have to have Occult, though, because Knowledges don't allow for defaults.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T08:37:09-07:00","id":1542910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it uses Occult, they actually have to have Occult, though, because Knowledges don't allow for defaults. </div> </div> </div>The three examples I gave have very high Occult (Goratrix and Baba Yaga, for instance would roll 16+ dice for countermagick and that is not even funny) and there isn't any powerful kindred woth his salt who hasn't Occult in his character sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T10:14:20-07:00","id":1542917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients?p=1542907#post1542907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Primium isn't so impressive, though that's another problem with having people who don't do math designing systems (difficulty 8 is a rather high hurdle for the paltry sum of dice that primium usually gives; even doubled successes can't compensate for that).</div> </div> </div> </div>And it goes back to the previous point: from a narrative point of view, Primium is fucking impressive, and one of the best kept secret of the Technocracy. The system fails to make it so, but lore-wise it's big stuff.<br /> Granted, however, most mages who encounter a Primium-covered hit-mark tend to last a short time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Time for a party. Time for lawn chairs! </div> </div> </div>Yes, the notorious lawn chairs is the perfect example of what I was talking about. Satyros has devoted an entire section in the M20 manual to explaining why it is a stupid idea for stupid players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I assume that this was just the perception of V:tM writers viewing it as the &quot;main line&quot; and trying to get everyone to donate to their lotion fund. </div> </div> </div>It does not change that the narrative canon is that<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How much later are we talking? It became horridly difficult for vampires of all generations to soak agg in Revised, and V20 didn't change that. The assumption seems to be &quot;even if you're an ancient, stay in the background or something is going to cap your ass.&quot; </div> </div> </div><br /> Again it is a gap in mechanics, the narrative fact remains.<br /> <br /> <br /> The 20th edition between the rules introduced in Mage to limit the power Mages have over Vampires and Werewolves and certain rule revisions in Vampire and Werewolf made a commendable effort to rebalance the system. Obviously with that source material it was not possible to do as CofD did, but the intent is there.<br /> <br /> But just to say: the Robustness of Vampire Dark Ages 20th edition is the strongest version ever, just as the Celerity of Masquerade 20th is absolutely broken, between the fact that with 1 blood point you can do as many actions as your value in Discipline or the fact that it adds to all rolls that have dexterity, thus including attacks and dodges. Menele with V20 rules does 10 actions with 1 roll 24 dice to attack, before pumping up with blood of course.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mechanically, it is hard to believe that it took an entire Sept of Werewolves to beat Vladimir Rustovich and that half a dozen elder Garou died in the battle. But it is a narrative fact, occurring in a Werewolf manual. And it goes back to my previous point.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200b<br /> If it uses Occult, they actually have to have Occult, though, because Knowledges don't allow for defaults. </div> </div> </div>Find me three Methuselahs who between Wits and Occult have less than 8 dice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-30-2024, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T11:16:35-07:00","id":1542918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients?p=1542910#post1542910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The three examples I gave have very high Occult (Goratrix and Baba Yaga, for instance would roll 16+ dice for countermagick and that is not even funny) and there isn't any powerful kindred woth his salt who hasn't Occult in his character sheet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. They had the time to branch out. Lots of other characters might not; you can reasonably expect some characters to pump dots into it because of mechanical incentives if nothing else, but it doesn't actually make it so that every character has it, and it still doesn't guarantee that they have good counters (again, if you're comparing it to primium, you might be overselling it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T12:45:17-07:00","id":1542923,"title":"","content":"Elders who do not have high values between occult and wits are very rare, even considering non-occult clans<br /> <br /> <br /> Xaviar 9<br /> Theo Bell 8<br /> Lodin 5<br /> Victoria Ash 8<br /> Art Morgan 10<br /> Dutch 5<br /> Pendragon 6<br /> Cicatriz 8<br /> Warwick 5<br /> Leigh 7<br /> Hardestadt 7<br /> Calebros 7<br /> Carlack 7<br /> Lady Ann 9<br /> Cock Robin 8<br /> Madame Guil 8<br /> Pascek 6<br /> Smiling Jack 7<br /> Ecaterina 7<br /> MacNeil 7<br /> Don Cerro 8<br /> Garinson 7<br /> Khalid 9<br /> Malachite 8<br /> Parovitch 9<br /> Tyler 7<br /> Balthazar 7<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if we consider Clans that from mechanics use occult like Tremere, Assamite, Malkavian, Lasombra, Tzimisce, Giovanni and so on we easily reach an average of 10<br /> <br /> Normally a Hit-Mark has between 4 and 5 countermagic dice. This means that the average elder is way more immune to magic than the average Hit-mark","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-30-2024, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T13:10:24-07:00","id":1542928,"title":"","content":"It's only a matter of time when a Kindred has to learn skills that will make them better at surviving there new state and what else is out there that could harm them and it wouldn't be all that unheard of them that your typical young anceilla has picked up at least 2 dots in Occult, Brawl, Melee, and Survival or Firearms skills and the older ones should have at least a 3 in one of them before they reach elder status.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T13:10:33-07:00","id":1542929,"title":"","content":"When most people talk about Ancients, you see the likes of Mithras, Menele, Helena, Baba Yaga, and Ur-Shulgi. Sure they've been pretty prominent across splats and supplements, but what about the other blood gods we don't talk about as much. The ones that don't get the bad guy of the week half ass stat treatment. Ravnos' Chandraputra and Hazimal. Tzimisce's Kartarirya and Demdemeh. Malkav's half dozen childer. Whoever's left in the other clans I can't be assed to look up at the moment. I really wish many of these other ancients got more of a role in the lore, as many of them could have been scary as shit. The tiny amount of power that Hazimal and Chandraputra showed in BJD, really highlighted the potential of the destruction such beings could cause if they really flexed.<br /> <br /> On the other topic here of Ascension Magic vs Kindred. It makes sense that Kindred would be more resistant to the influence of Ascension Magic as they are &quot;natural&quot; part of Static Reality. They and their abilities don't incur Paradox, and so Reality should favor them over things like Hit-Marks which are Reality aberrations just for existing at least until the Technocracy some how changes the Paradigm .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-30T15:30:41-07:00","id":1542937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients?p=1542923#post1542923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elders who do not have high values between occult and wits are very rare, even considering non-occult clans<br /> <br /> <br /> Xaviar 9<br /> Theo Bell 8<br /> Lodin 5<br /> Victoria Ash 8<br /> Art Morgan 10<br /> Dutch 5<br /> Pendragon 6<br /> Cicatriz 8<br /> Warwick 5<br /> Leigh 7<br /> Hardestadt 7<br /> Calebros 7<br /> Carlack 7<br /> Lady Ann 9<br /> Cock Robin 8<br /> Madame Guil 8<br /> Pascek 6<br /> Smiling Jack 7<br /> Ecaterina 7<br /> MacNeil 7<br /> Don Cerro 8<br /> Garinson 7<br /> Khalid 9<br /> Malachite 8<br /> Parovitch 9<br /> Tyler 7<br /> Balthazar 7<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if we consider Clans that from mechanics use occult like Tremere, Assamite, Malkavian, Lasombra, Tzimisce, Giovanni and so on we easily reach an average of 10<br /> <br /> Normally a Hit-Mark has between 4 and 5 countermagic dice. This means that the average elder is way more immune to magic than the average Hit-mark</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, exactly. And many of these are not even &quot;Elders&quot; per se (e.g. Theo Bell). So, you see my main concern is balance. As I cited in my other post, while it makes absolutely no sense to me to see some poorly designed Gifts like Pawn of the Newborn's Cub taking effect against any other splat without a resist roll, this case is more about the Gift being a terribly designed one. Because on the other hand, it feels a bit too much when one side has such a huge advantage resisting the powers of another splat and I feel that's what happens when we use the Night-Folk Countermagic as it is in the books. It's just unfair, I think one good and simple solution would be to have something like a Willpower roll to resist, that's probably the best solution among the ones I've tested, but still it gives vampires a perhaps too good resistance, so perhaps something like just Occult would be better. I'm still far from satisfied in this regard, tbh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-01T19:41:09-07:00","id":1542990,"title":"","content":"I think VtM Revised Storyteller's Handbook had the best system for vampires countering mage spells (roll Thaumaturgy rating against difficulty equal to mage's Willpower; Thaumaturgical Countermagic adds one die per dot). One's ability to shrug off true magic depended on how much expertise and power one had at vampiric sorcery, rather than general occult scholarship and quick thinking in the hands of any vampire, even one with no practical ability in that arena.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T11:37:16-07:00","id":1543020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients?p=1542990#post1542990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think VtM Revised Storyteller's Handbook had the best system for vampires countering mage spells (roll Thaumaturgy rating against difficulty equal to mage's Willpower; Thaumaturgical Countermagic adds one die per dot). One's ability to shrug off true magic depended on how much expertise and power one had at vampiric sorcery, rather than general occult scholarship and quick thinking in the hands of any vampire, even one with no practical ability in that arena.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I also think it's the best alternative in the sense that it's the one that makes more sense, I have used this one often in my tables, but then there are some who complain about &quot;Tremere too op nerf pls&quot;. I think the passive countermagick should be only against things like turning a vampire into a lawn chair and the like, even though I also like the idea in M20 that any vampire with knowledge in Protean/Vicissitude and other powers that allow him to change form, should be able to revert the transformation with ease. Fortunately in my many years of crossover experience no mage tried to turn a vampire in anything like that, normally they prefer the &quot;fireball approach&quot; and then a Blood Sorcerer with enough knowledge of the magic arts should be able to try to counter it, but I don't think someone without such knowledges should have any other &quot;naural defense&quot; like &quot;night-folk countermagick&quot; in this case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T17:45:44-07:00","id":1543042,"title":"","content":"I don't think any particular method is the best, it depends.<br /> <br /> At my current chronicle, which is actually Mage, I plan on using Occult, maybe with Blood Sorcery having an easier time.<br /> <br /> Putting aside whatever that may or may not make sense (Vampires are already magical beings that can still exist on Earth, I find it hard to believe they can\u2019t have innate magical protection), I do that because I want Vampires to be relevant when they show up, and they\u2019ll be central to two or three important side plots.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I see those systems together as dials to get the exact result you want. Without some form of countermagick, dealing with Vampires is trivial for most Mages. Having a default makes the vampires more relevant. Defaulting to Willpower is interesting as an option actually focused on dealing with other splats, a game about supernatural mystery where survival is not guaranteed. If you want to make Paradox a big theme in your game, it is even possible that the other splats have Permadox that don\u2019t affect them, but affects Mages nearby.<br /> <br /> So, options. They make for different interactions that are good at different chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T05:26:35-07:00","id":1543055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients?p=1543042#post1543042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think any particular method is the best, it depends.<br /> <br /> At my current chronicle, which is actually Mage, I plan on using Occult, maybe with Blood Sorcery having an easier time.<br /> <br /> Putting aside whatever that may or may not make sense (Vampires are already magical beings that can still exist on Earth, I find it hard to believe they can\u2019t have innate magical protection), I do that because I want Vampires to be relevant when they show up, and they\u2019ll be central to two or three important side plots.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I see those systems together as dials to get the exact result you want. Without some form of countermagick, dealing with Vampires is trivial for most Mages. Having a default makes the vampires more relevant. Defaulting to Willpower is interesting as an option actually focused on dealing with other splats, a game about supernatural mystery where survival is not guaranteed. If you want to make Paradox a big theme in your game, it is even possible that the other splats have Permadox that don\u2019t affect them, but affects Mages nearby.<br /> <br /> So, options. They make for different interactions that are good at different chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very interesting take. I don't really think there's any inherent metaphysical problem with vampires having natural countermagick. My main concern is balance, because as I stated, the table turn completely if we allow every vampire to use wits+ occult to countermagick. Of course I'm not talking about the average neonate and fledglings, but once we have elders (or even some ancillae, like Theo Bell) if every vampire has such a dicepool to countermagic mages become trivial to them. And on top of that we already have the fact that mages are much more fragile than vampires, so imagine a vampire with celerity (I mean, I don't use standard rules, nor multiple actions, because they utterly break the ST system, but many people, probably most and with it celerity is absolutely broken) and an innate countermagick that doesn't even cost an action and then we have a problem, a serious one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T20:41:43-07:00","id":1543081,"title":"","content":"I have to agree with the notion that maybe 4th and maybe 5th generation kindred shouldn't be stated to create a sense of vast power that the weaker vampires can't begin to understand or match even if someone like Montano who is willing to teach others about Oblivion but has limits of what can be taught because of the huge power difference between a 4th generation ancient and a 10th-13th generation ancillae or neonates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T05:43:04-07:00","id":1543091,"title":"","content":"I don't think its a balance issue. Mages, in the Ascension books are always stated to be just utterly human. Yes they are human with god-like powers to shape reality and cause anything they can imagine to happen, happen, with the consequence of major undertakings causing reality to snap back with paradox, but they are, and will always be just human. This means they can die just like any other human their magic non withstanding. They're the glass cannons of the splats.<br /> <br /> The other splat creatures, are all an accepted part of that reality (according to reality itself..) that the Mages are manipulating, so it should take more effort to effect a sentient being than say a pipe on a wall.<br /> <br /> TBH there's a lot in the D10 system that WoD uses that is pretty unbalanced, so the best bet is to just take what you find and change it to suit your needs. Vamps having too big dice pools with Occult + Wits? Half it. Gives them some sort of resistance, and keeps it to more manageable levels. (So a theoretical 4th gen Methuselah would have a max pool of 9 instead of 18.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-04T12:01:18-07:00","id":1543114,"title":"","content":"I arrived very late to the conversation, but let's go anyway. In my headcanon, taking the antediluvians as a base, I think that fourth and fifth generation kindreds (maybe some from the sixth) would have very problematic abilities to deal with even in groups and even experienced garou would have to be very careful when dealing with them.<br /> <br /> Things like Gangrels capable of transforming into powerful chimeras composed of several animals or transforming into a fog capable of sucking the blood present like a cloud of mosquitoes within a given area, not an entire city of course, but perhaps a building or a street; Tzimice capable of merging with their territory or transforming their bodies in very bizarre ways; Ravnos capable of creating illusions with real consequences, even &quot;recreating&quot; kindreds that have already been destroyed or creatures that exist only in legends.<br /> <br /> Ok, kind of absurd, but I think you get my point, strong and problematic to face even if you disregard the resources they must have acquired over the years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T17:20:35-07:00","id":1543174,"title":"","content":"After thinking about this subject, something came to my mind, would a chronicle where one of the PCs came from a lineage created by chimerstry be functional?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T20:49:39-07:00","id":1543182,"title":"","content":"Perhaps if it was the Ravnos itself or his oldest and strongest childer Psicose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-05T23:58:48-07:00","id":1543187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients?p=1543081#post1543081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to agree with the notion that maybe 4th and maybe 5th generation kindred shouldn't be stated to create a sense of vast power that the weaker vampires can't begin to understand or match even if someone like Montano who is willing to teach others about Oblivion but has limits of what can be taught because of the huge power difference between a 4th generation ancient and a 10th-13th generation ancillae or neonates.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would normaly agree with you. At least in most chronicles, however, when I ST an Elder's story I feel the need to give them Stasi.<br /> In any case, I agree that when we're STing stories for neonates, it's definitely not necessary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I arrived very late to the conversation, but let's go anyway. In my headcanon, taking the antediluvians as a base, I think that fourth and fifth generation kindreds (maybe some from the sixth) would have very problematic abilities to deal with even in groups and even experienced garou would have to be very careful when dealing with them.<br /> <br /> Things like Gangrels capable of transforming into powerful chimeras composed of several animals or transforming into a fog capable of sucking the blood present like a cloud of mosquitoes within a given area, not an entire city of course, but perhaps a building or a street; Tzimice capable of merging with their territory or transforming their bodies in very bizarre ways; Ravnos capable of creating illusions with real consequences, even &quot;recreating&quot; kindreds that have already been destroyed or creatures that exist only in legends.<br /> <br /> Ok, kind of absurd, but I think you get my point, strong and problematic to face even if you disregard the resources they must have acquired over the years. </div> </div> </div>I certainly get what you mean and I agree in many ways, I just think that when they have such a huge dice pool advantage when it comes to dealing with other splats, it can get problematic especially if we have a group composed of different splats, like I often have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T13:13:54-07:00","id":1543209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients?p=1543182#post1543182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps if it was the Ravnos itself or his oldest and strongest childer Psicose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was talking about its use in the game, because on one hand it's an interesting detail, but on the other it might not be very useful. To make that clear, I think a fourth or fifth generation Methuselah would be capable of this if he had enough understanding of the discipline, I mean, I imagine that once the object became real it stabilizes until the Methuselah undoes it. This would even leave open whether the Ravnos clan itself as a whole wouldn't be a creation of the antediluvian's discipline, yes I'm traveling with this theory more than I should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T14:42:41-07:00","id":1543214,"title":"","content":"Interesting notion .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-28T20:54:22-08:00","id":1557977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Carsusbloodking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients#post1540024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How dangerous are the elders and methuselahs really? In the lore it has elders being movers and shakers of entire regions to entire continent's, and yet they seem to die in droves against everything from neonates, to garou, to mages. So is it all just propaganda or do the ancients really have some bite to them?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, it's a Mage.<br /> <br /> You've got Blood Sorcerers out here cursing entire clans and bloodlines. So a fully awakened Mage should be several orders of magnitude more dangerous.<br /> <br /> As for the Methuselahs, I've heard several accounts in which their discipline mastery was so high, they could effectively replicate a Dragon Ball fight scene. Speed blitzing their way across continents, or shaking entire mountains with the force of their punches. At a high enough level of mastery with Fortitude, you can just tank direct exposure to sunlight; though you might still have difficulty staying awake.<br /> <br /> <br /> Methuselahs are more than just mere vampires, they're minor demigods in their own right. So it's probably a good thing that most of them are spending their time in torpor, instead of actively roaming the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-27T10:17:40-07:00","id":1562229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1540024-powers-of-the-ancients?p=1543209#post1543209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was talking about its use in the game, because on one hand it's an interesting detail, but on the other it might not be very useful. To make that clear, I think a fourth or fifth generation Methuselah would be capable of this if he had enough understanding of the discipline, I mean, I imagine that once the object became real it stabilizes until the Methuselah undoes it. This would even leave open whether the Ravnos clan itself as a whole wouldn't be a creation of the antediluvian's discipline, yes I'm traveling with this theory more than I should.</div> </div> </div> </div>By crossover rules found in Changeling, what is created with Chimerstry, even at low levels, has some endurance as a Chimerical object after the illusion is dismissed.<br /> <br /> Chimeras exist in many forms, and their birth is not a predictable phenomenon. Sometimes a minor event creates very powerful Chimeras.<br /> <br /> There are Chimeras with strange powers, with poison, diseases or curses, some capable of visual manifestation to people and some can become tangible to normal humans.<br /> <br /> So... Yeah, actually you don't need much for a Chimerstry user to accidentally create a new progenitor for a Bloodline or Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-27T11:39:26-07:00","id":1562231,"title":"","content":"Impressive that we have ressurcted a necro thread.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T08:12:56-07:00","id":1562559,"title":"","content":"When comparing vampire elders to mages, though, you forget one important detail. <br /> <br /> Mages are still mortal, still human, with all the human foibles. They're also subject to paradox, elder vampires are not.<br /> <br /> So really, the answer to the question of &quot;who wins, vampire methuselah or awakened archmage?&quot; is &quot;Whoever goes first.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T09:26:05-07:00","id":1562563,"title":"","content":"It certainly didn't work for the number of 4th generation Banu Haqim ancients when they tried to kill Al-Ashrad when he was still mortal and he took them out without a cut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-03T17:14:31-07:00","id":1562597,"title":"","content":"Because that's a story, not an implementation of the rules, and this particular story wanted to give him awesomeness.<br /> <br /> Also technically a Mage can do that I'd they prepared for such a situation beforehand. The problem with Mage is that, in the end, there's nothing you can say for sure preemptively.<br /> <br /> What a Mage can do? Anything, including fail hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-04T09:51:28-07:00","id":1562656,"title":"","content":"That is true about making a mortal Asrad being already a potent mage with incredible skill before being embraced into Banu Haqim by Ur-Shugi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-06T07:09:22-07:00","id":1562772,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that al-Ashrad was powerful enough and bold enough to be in conflict with Haqim himself. From <i>&quot;Children of the Night&quot;</i>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The greatest magician in the world went to the chambers of the Ancestor and spoke of what had happened. What transpired there none can say for certain, but the stories tell of a mighty argument, of al-Ashrad's accusations that the Ancestor had sought to bind his powers to the service of the Children, thoughtless of the sorcerer's freedom. Haqim's anger was no less, for the first of those al-Ashrad had slain was his favorite and most trusted son. The Ancestor's belief was that the magician had sought to usurp that childe's position as his right hand.<br /> <br /> Both mighty creatures' spines stiffened with pride, and they might have come to blows had no ur-Shulgi, Haqim's second son, intervened. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}